WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:04.670
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:05.503
- What up, guys?

00:00:05.503 --> 00:00:07.070
Helen here to talk about the film

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.570
that convinced you to create
a new fake Gmail account

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.190
so you could try to nab another one

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.360
of those recently
discontinued HBO Max trials.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.260
That's right, "Wonder Woman 1984."

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.580
Now, like most of you, we were big fans

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.720
of the first "Wonder Woman"

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.700
and we're naturally
stoked about the sequel.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.010
And while plenty of people
thought the movie was fun,

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.970
others were a little disappointed.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.470
And while people might
want to nitpick plot holes

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:30.750
or action sequences,

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.850
we at Wisecrack thought
we'd try to learn something

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.207
about screenwriting by
asking the question,

00:00:35.207 --> 00:00:38.410
"'Wonder Woman 1984,' what went wrong?"

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.360
And of course, spoilers
ahead for a brand new movie

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.490
and a rather old British story.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.120
But before we get into it,

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.740
I wanted to take a second to tell you

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.800
about Wisecrack's Patreon page,

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.810
which is sort of like a secret island

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:53.500
of highly trained Amazons
but for people who can't help

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.670
but search for meaning in pop culture.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.040
So nothing like a secret island
of highly trained Amazons,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.720
but hey, you can join for as little as $2,

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.330
which is also how much it cost
for a set of snap bracelets

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.660
back in 1984.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.860
Along with early access
to ad-free versions

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:11.300
of all of our videos, patrons
have access to our Discord,

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.570
a place to compare notes
about recent videos,

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:16.030
